# Mo Li Hua (Jasmine Flower) (repertoire plan: mo-li-hua). The Jiangsu folk tune as it is
# commonly sung or played today (older printings vary), from the folk song only: Puccini quotes it
# in Turandot (1926), but nothing here comes from Puccini. This is the first half of the verse:
# bars 1-16 of the 17 bars that independent recollections agreed on note for note (bar 17 only
# opens the next phrase, so it is left out). Four four-bar phrases, the first three resting on D,
# the fourth coming home to G. The second half of the verse, with its closing cadence, was not
# agreed and is left out rather than guessed. No words: played as an instrumental.
# Every note is one of the five notes of G major pentatonic: G A B D E.
# Played an octave below the sung pitch (so it reads like the song in the treble clef), in seventh
# position on strings 4, 3 and 2: finger 1 on fret 7, finger 2 on fret 8, finger 3 on fret 9.
# A = string 4 fret 7, B = string 4 fret 9, D = string 3 fret 7, E = string 3 fret 9,
# G = string 2 fret 8. In bar 15 finger 1 slides down string 4 to fret 5 for the low G, and the
# hand stays there (A = string 4 fret 7 with finger 3).
# Played twice, the same notes and rhythm both times: first plain, then with ornaments. The second
# time the D-E and B-A-B turns are slurred (hammer-ons and pull-offs, pick only the first note),
# each long D is a light slide up from two frets below, picked on the beat like a grace note, and
# the last G is a slide down from A.
# The teacher strums G, C, D and Em, two strums a bar and one under each long note.
title: Mo Li Hua (Jasmine Flower)
id: mo-li-hua
composer: Traditional Chinese (Jiangsu)
source: Jiangsu folk tune of the 18th century, printed in Europe by 1804; melody as commonly sung today, first half of the verse; arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (traditional); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 4
tags: melody, chinese, major pentatonic, slides, hammer-on, pull-off, position shift
tempo: 66
time: 2/4
key: G

